+   "body": "Summary of investigation so far (steps 1-2):\n\nFiles read:\n- config/shipping-api.yaml is the repo default for build 4.31.3. It is STALE and superseded by the deploy log. It says database.pool.max_size: 40 (line 10), min_idle: 4 (line 11), acquire_timeout_ms: 5000 (line 12), db host shipping-api-db.internal (line 8). Line 2 says deploy-time overrides are recorded in deploy/changes.log.\n- deploy/changes.log:14 is AUTHORITATIVE: \"2031-04-21T08:28:20Z CHG-4162 APPLIED  shipping-api override db.pool.max_size=12 (was 40) by deploy-bot; reason: align with shared-db connection quota\". The effective pool max_size is therefore 12.\n- deploy/changes.log:15 is CHG-4163, PROPOSED at 2031-04-21T08:52:08Z: shipping-api db.pool.max_size=56. It was not applied, so ignore it as effective config. It does suggest the intended fix value.\n- Other change-log lines concern other services and are irrelevant. These are CHG-4149 to CHG-4161 and CHG-4164: returns, orders, payments, fulfil, catalog, inventory, profile and quotes.\n- ops/oncall-notes.md is informal and stale.\n  - Line 5 (08:12) claims max_size 40. This predates CHG-4162 and is wrong.\n  - Line 6 notes a cert warning for shipping-api.internal that is \"weeks away\". This makes TLS_CERT_EXPIRED unlikely.\n  - Line 7 (08:36) records the 503s and suspects rates-svc slowness.\n  - Line 8 says upstream dashboards look normal.\n\nLog and metric evidence:\n- logs/shipping-api.log before the change shows db pool stats in_use around 4-8 (e.g. lines 5, 62, 65, 74, 106, 155, 184, 214, from 07:30 to 07:50). That is above 12 in no case but near it.\n- logs/ingress-a.log has 503 errors with upstream_error=\"upstream timeout\" for upstream=shipping-api starting at line 272 (2031-04-21T08:31:58.596Z), shortly after CHG-4162 at 08:28:20. Further examples are at lines 275, 276, 282, 285, 287, 290 and 294.\n- metrics/shipping-api.csv has columns minute,rps,p99_ms,db_pool_in_use,cpu_pct.\n  - Line 60 (08:28): p99 115, pool 4.\n  - Line 80 (08:48): p99 3306, pool_in_use 12, which is pinned at the new cap.\n  - Line 100 (09:08): p99 3113, pool 12.\n  - Line 120 (09:28): p99 4241, pool 12.\n  - CPU is normal (about 40-53%).\n\nCurrent conclusion (strongly supported):\n- root_cause: DB_POOL_EXHAUSTED. The APPLIED override CHG-4162 cut shipping-api db.pool.max_size from 40 to 12. The pool saturates at 12, latency spikes and ingress-a gets upstream timeouts (503s).\n- required_value: 12\n- remedy: RAISE_DB_POOL_LIMIT. Raise shipping-api db.pool.max_size above demand (e.g. back to 40 or the proposed 56), coordinating with the shared-db quota.\n- Ruled out or unlikely:\n  - TLS: the cert is weeks from expiry.\n  - Rates-svc slowness: dashboards normal.\n  - CPU: normal.\n\nPlanned next steps, optional before answering:\n- Grep shipping-api.log after 08:28 for pool-exhaustion or acquire-timeout errors and get exact line numbers.\n- Find the exact metrics line range where db_pool_in_use first hits 12, roughly lines 61-80.\n\nDraft evidence_refs:\n- deploy/changes.log:14\n- config/shipping-api.yaml:10\n- logs/ingress-a.log:272-294\n- metrics/shipping-api.csv:60-80\n- plus the shipping-api.log error lines once found"
